course: dictionary
lesson: 8724
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Separation is a noun, and it can mean different things. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Draining pasta is a separation» is about a mixture being split into its parts, because the colander lets the water through but keeps the pasta.
explain: Separation can also mean the space or distance between things. Or it can be about people. «Divorce or separation means parents stop being a couple; they are still both the child's parents.» Here separation means a time when parents no longer live together, but the child still has both of them.
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. For the pasta, splitting a mixture fits. For the parents, stopping being a couple fits. The clues in the sentence show you which meaning to choose.
fact: Separation means moving things apart, keeping them apart, or the space between things.
fact: In science, separation means splitting a mixture into its parts, by filtering, sieving or evaporating.
fact: «Draining pasta is a separation: the holes of the colander are big enough for water but too small for the pasta.»
fact: When parents stop living together, this is also called separation, and they are still both the child's parents.
fact: «Separation of powers» means splitting power between the lawmakers, the government and the courts, so no one part gets too strong.
exercise: «Draining pasta is a separation: the holes of the colander are big enough for water but too small for the pasta.» What is being separated here? | *Water and pasta | The colander and the sink | Pasta and sauce | The holes and the bowl
exercise: «Divorce or separation means parents stop being a couple; they are still both the child's parents.» What does separation mean here? | Parents swap their children | *Parents stop being a couple, but both are still parents | Parents argue about money all the time | Parents go on holiday together
exercise: Which of these is a separation in science? | *Sieving sand out of water | Counting to ten | Walking to school | Hugging a friend
test: «Separation of powers» means splitting power between the lawmakers, the government and the courts. What does separation mean here? | *Splitting power into parts so no one gets too strong | Joining all the powers together | Moving the courts to a new city | Making the government bigger
test: «There was a wide separation between the two trees.» What does separation mean here? | A kind of wood used for furniture | Leaves falling from the branches | The two trees growing together | *The space between them
exam: Which meaning fits «Draining pasta is a separation»? | Making the pasta longer | *Splitting a mixture into its parts | Covering the pasta in sauce | Adding more water to the pan
